From: Gentoo optimization <optimization@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] retain the historical OpenUrlJob compatibility data symbol

Keep the data symbol exported by the previous KIO ABI.  It is retained for
already-linked consumers; the current implementation does not need to read it.

--- a/src/gui/openurljob.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/openurljob.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@
 #include <QOperatingSystemVersion>
 #include <mimetypefinderjob.h>
 
+// Kept for ABI compatibility with KIO 6.27 and earlier consumers.
+extern "C" KIOGUI_EXPORT bool openurljob_force_use_browserapp_kdeglobals = false;
+
 // A file:// URL may carry a host that names the local machine (RFC 8089), e.g.
 // those produced by `ls --hyperlink` or Midnight Commander's OSC 8 sequences.
 // Strip such a host so the URL becomes a plain local path: QUrl::toLocalFile()
